---
import PlaygroundShell from '../../components/PlaygroundShell.astro';
import RangeField from '../../components/RangeField.astro';
---
<PlaygroundShell title="Back-of-the-envelope numbers" hint="How many KeepAlive calls the master must answer, how long a dead client's lock stays held, how much of the grace period a fail-over uses, and how many replica failures a cell survives. A teaching model with round numbers, not Google's data.">
  <div class="pg est" data-est>
    <div class="pg-row">
      <RangeField label="Clients (thousands)" name="c" min="1" max="100" step="1" value="90" />
      <RangeField label="Session lease (seconds)" name="l" min="6" max="60" step="1" value="12" />
      <RangeField label="Election time after a master fails (seconds)" name="e" min="2" max="40" step="1" value="6" />
      <RangeField label="Grace period (seconds)" name="g" min="5" max="90" step="5" value="45" />
      <RangeField label="Replicas in the cell" name="r" min="3" max="9" step="2" value="5" />
      <RangeField label="Files each client keeps cached" name="f" min="1" max="1000" step="1" value="50" />
      <RangeField label="Writes to files each second (thousands)" name="w" min="0.1" max="20" step="0.1" value="1" />
    </div>
    <dl class="est-out" data-out aria-live="polite"></dl>
    <p class="pg-note">Teaching model, not Google's system or data. From the Chubby paper: the default session lease is 12 seconds and an overloaded master may use up to about 60, the default grace period is 45 seconds, a cell has five replicas of which three must be running, two recent elections took 6 s and 4 s (up to 30 s), and 90,000 clients have talked to one master. The write rate, the files cached per client and the other values are my guesses that you can change. Assumptions: each client sends one KeepAlive per lease (the master holds each call until the lease is nearly over, so there is almost always one waiting), every write invalidates the cached copies of the file in a few clients, and the dead client's lock is released only when its lease ends.</p>
  </div>
</PlaygroundShell>
<script>
  import { query, numberValue, formatOneDecimalBelow100 } from '../../playground';
  document.querySelectorAll<HTMLElement>('[data-est]').forEach((root) => {
    const q = query(root);
    const val = numberValue(q);
    const OUT_ROWS = 10; // lines in the result list
    const rows = Array.from({ length: OUT_ROWS }, () => { const dt = document.createElement('dt'); const dd = document.createElement('dd'); q('[data-out]').append(dt, dd); return { dt, dd }; });
    const f1 = formatOneDecimalBelow100;
    const pct = (n: number) => `${(Math.round(n * 1000) / 1000).toLocaleString('en-US')}%`;
    function draw() {
      ['c', 'l', 'e', 'g', 'r', 'f', 'w'].forEach((key) => (q(`[data-${key}val]`).textContent = String(val(`[data-${key}]`))));
      const clients = val('[data-c]') * 1000; const lease = val('[data-l]'); const election = val('[data-e]'); const grace = val('[data-g]');
      const replicas = val('[data-r]'); const files = val('[data-f]'); const writes = val('[data-w]') * 1000;
      const majority = Math.floor(replicas / 2) + 1;
      const data: [string, string][] = [
        ['KeepAlive calls the master answers each second', f1(clients / lease)],
        ['KeepAlive calls a minute', f1((clients / lease) * 60)],
        ['Calls each second if the lease were 60 seconds instead', f1(clients / 60)],
        ['Longest a dead holder keeps its lock (seconds)', f1(lease)],
        ['Time left in the grace period when the new master answers (seconds)', election <= grace ? f1(grace - election) : 'none: the session is lost'],
        ['Does a client keep its session through the fail-over?', election <= grace ? 'yes' : 'no'],
        ['Cached files across all clients (millions)', f1((clients * files) / 1e6)],
        ['Invalidation messages each second, if 5 clients cache each written file', f1(writes * 5)],
        ['Replicas needed for the cell to be up', String(majority)],
        ['Replica failures the cell survives', String(replicas - majority)],
      ];
      rows.forEach((r, i) => { r.dt.textContent = data[i][0]; r.dd.textContent = data[i][1]; });
    }
    root.addEventListener('input', draw);
    draw();
  });
</script>
